// Game reputations start at 1000

{1000}{Reputation example.}
{1001}{Member of the Thieves Underground. This enables you to buy from black market stores and get free information and leads on jobs from other members.}
{1002}{Member of the Clan Maug. As such, you are a sworn enemy of the Pollock Gang, and there is a fair chance that they will attack you on sight.}
{1003}{Member of the Pollock Gang. As such, you are a sworn enemy of the Clan Maug, and there is a fair chance that they will attack you on sight.}
{1004}{Betrayer of the Clan Maug. Members of the Clan Maug will generally attack you on sight.}
{1005}{You have trained as a Master Healer with Kal-N'driel in Quintarra. You are respected and admired in Quintarra and favorably regarded in all other major cities.}
{1006}{You have murdered Kal-N'driel, the Healing Master. An act of infamy that has earned you hatred of all in Quintarra.}
{1007}{You have killed the beautiful Clarissa Shalmo the Throwing Master of Caladon. You have earned the disfavor of the guards of Caladon.}
{1008}{Pervert of Tarant. Your exhibitionist antics in Tarant have earned you the scorn of its citizens.} 
{1009}{You owe Gurin Rockharrow 5000 coins for gambling debts.}
{1010}{You have defaulted on your gambling debt with Gurin Rockharrow.}
{1011}{You are known as the betrayer of Tarant's beloved Gilbert Bates. As such, you find the citizens of Tarant a bit less cordial toward you than they once were.}
{1012}{Bow Master of Arcanum. Your skill with a bow is unmatched.}
{1013}{Dodge Master of Arcanum. You have been trained by Adkin Chambers in Mastery of the Dodge.}
{1014}{Melee Master of Arcanum. Your skill in melee combat is supreme.}
{1015}{Throwing Master of Arcanum. Training with Clarissa Shalmo has made you the throwing Master.}
{1016}{Gambling Master of Arcanum.}
{1017}{Haggle Master of Arcanum. Your dealings with J.M. Morat have gained you the title of Haggle Master.}
{1018}{Persuasion Master of Arcanum. Your repuatation for oratory and negotiation is legendary.}
{1019}{Repair Master of Arcanum. Your brilliance with technological things is widely acclaimed.}
{1020}{Firearms Master of Arcanum. Your skill with firearms is unmatched.}
{1021}{Master Locksmith of Arcanum. Your understanding of locking mechanisms is unsurpassed in Arcanum.}
{1022}{Trap Master of Arcanum. Surviving Daniel McPherson's training has earned you fame and recognition as a Master of arming and disarming traps.}
{1023}{Enemy of Qintarra.}
{1024}{Friend of the Molochean Hand}
{1025}{As the infamous Butcher of Stillwater, you will find that most citizens of the larger cities of Arcanum will have a dislike of you.}
